@startuml UC-003-analysis-class
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
hide empty members
hide circle
title UC-003 Execute target model: analysis class diagram (BCE)

class "Target Model Interface" as TMI <<boundary>> {
  send question
}
class "Progress Listener" as PLis <<boundary>> {
  case executed(target result)
}
class "Execute Target" as Exec <<control>> {
  execute(benchmark, target)
  stop reason
}
class "Benchmark" as B <<entity>> {
  test cases, in order
}
class "Test Case" as TC <<entity>> {
  id
  question
}
class "Target Result" as TR <<entity>> {
  test case
  model response or connector error
}
class "Model Response" as MR <<entity>> {
  text or refusal
  truncated
  requested and served model
}
class "Connector Error" as CE <<entity>> {
  kind
  message
}

Exec --> B : reads
B *-- "1..*" TC
Exec --> TMI : sends through
Exec --> TR : creates, one per case
Exec --> PLis : tells
TR --> "1" TC : for
TR --> "0..1" MR : holds
TR --> "0..1" CE : holds
TMI ..> MR : returns
TMI ..> CE : reports

note bottom of TR
  Exactly one of model response
  and connector error is present.
end note
note right of Exec
  Business rules: one call per case;
  an auth or quota error stops the run,
  and later cases are recorded "not sent".
end note
@enduml
